# Round xstream23 (R2 + R3): the one expert-stream owner (crates/gpu/src/host/xstream.rs) wired into Qwen3.8's
# ubatch walk. BLOOMERY_XSTREAM=split admits the residency pick (its floor the stream rule's m*, from the lane's
# probed rate) and then streams the host experts the rule (runtime::xsplit) sends to the card through a ring of
# card slots for the ubatch alone, cut at the ring's half and where the card's side (the pick's and the stream's
# copies on one lane, then the stacks' own columns and the streamed ones) would pass the union the host keeps.
# Same binary, every arm BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p148-s1 and BLOOMERY_DRAFT=off; split against off; admit (the
# shipped shape) read beside, not judged.
#
# Decomposition per layer of the one 4,096-column unit, A6000 plan a, prose. The round's functional run (same
# binary and levers, gpu-gate.sh on the A6000, not timed, the box shared with other rounds' gates) gives every
# term but the window's own scale:
#   off   the union of every host expert's columns: 19,350 slots a layer at 4.92 us = 95.2 ms, plus 30.4 ms a
#         layer waiting on the card's front -> walk 6.22 s, prompt 6.26 s functional; 6.64 s and pp4096 616.9
#         timed (rig-log 09-30, the q38seed arms).
#   split the pick admits 76.7 experts a layer (3,683), the stream takes 26.2 a layer of the rule's tail (1,258
#         over the 42 layers that streamed, at most 91 of the ring's half of 97) and 85,806 of their columns;
#         the union keeps 3,165 slots a layer (15.5 ms) while the card's shadow (the pick's and the stream's
#         copies at the probed 20.49 GB/s, then the route) takes ~28 ms: the walk is 62 ms a layer, card-bound
#         -> 3.03 s functional. Scaled by the off arm's timed/functional ratio (6.64 / 6.26): ~3.2 s timed,
#         pp4096 ~1,280.
#   A second functional run, 4,100 ids (a 4,096-column unit and a 4-column one the stream skips), gave split
#         3.10 s and off 5.37 s, the same 16 greedy ids: the off arm moves with the shared box's host load
#         (5.37-6.26 s) while split, card-bound, holds (3.03-3.10 s).
#   => split vs off +65..+120 % (the functional ratios +73 % and +106 %, the timed off arm's 6.64 s at the top).
#   admit beside it: q38seed measured +71.6 % (3.87 s); split moves ~1,258 more experts' columns to the card.
# The derivation before the functional run (+60..+80 %, split ~ admit) took the replay's post-pick union of
# 2,190 columns a layer; the live run keeps 5,165 a layer before the stream (3,165 kept + 2,000 streamed). That
# term was the miss.
# Runner (from /Users/hckim/repo/bloomery-xstream23, the full output to a file first):
# BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/xstream-pp.card BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4352' BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=4
# just depth-gpu-qwen4exp prose:4096@BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p148-s1,BLOOMERY_DRAFT=off,BLOOMERY_XSTREAM=off
#   prose:4096@BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p148-s1,BLOOMERY_DRAFT=off,BLOOMERY_XSTREAM=split
#   prose:4096@BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p148-s1,BLOOMERY_DRAFT=off,BLOOMERY_XSTREAM=admit
# Wall [derived]: 3 arms x 4 rounds of a fresh Qwen3.8 load (q38seed's 4 x 4 took 9-12 min), 7..10 min.
kind: ab
question: does the expert stream's split (the pick at the rule's floor, then the stream cut at the ring's half
  and the balance) lift Qwen3.8's pp4096 over the plain arm by the derived band, the shipped admit arm beside it?
term: pp tok/s @ prose:4096, ctx 4352 (BLOOMERY_GEN_CTX=4352), A6000, plan a, BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p148-s1 and
  BLOOMERY_DRAFT=off in every arm; BLOOMERY_XSTREAM=split against BLOOMERY_XSTREAM=off, same binary, paired by
  round; the BLOOMERY_XSTREAM=admit arm run beside, not judged
unit: %
predict: +65..+120
rounds: 4
sd: 0.6 % AGENTS.md 「Know the ruler」, same-binary paired ratio SD
condition: one binary, all arms in one lease, a fresh process per load group, the host set and the PLE table
  warm (majflt near 0), no [cpu-busy] or [other-busy] row; a functional run of the same binary and levers just
  before the window (gpu-gate.sh on the A6000, not timed, BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1) shows the split arm's
  `xstream=split` line with xstream_half at least 8, one `xstream` record a card layer of the 4,096-column
  ubatch, streamed at most min(tail, half), the records' host_columns summing to the `stat prompt host`
  host_slots, and the `xstream end` record with lane_gbs above 10; distinct tokens equal between the split and
  off arms within the band's greedy margin
decide-in: land split as the unset value; then the balance's host cost from the call's own union (the split
  arm's shadow runs ~28 ms against a 15.5 ms union a layer: the rule's 7.0 us a column against the measured
  4.9 over-streams) as its own card, and the common-machine card (docs/cards/xstream-common.card)
decide-below: read the split arm's `xstream` records and `stat prompt` lines before any change: streamed far
  under ~26 a layer means the half or the balance cut (lane_gbs names the lane); streamed near it with the walk
  long means the card's shadow binds harder than the functional run showed, which an nsys of one ubatch
  decomposes
decide-above: check distinct tokens and the off arm's union slots (~19,350 a layer) before believing it;
  re-derive the off arm's wait on the card's front first
